# Deployment step, not a config file: how adilet_ca_bundle.pem gets into
# ~/.hermes/monitoring/blackbox/, which docker-compose.yml.fragment mounts
# read-only into the blackbox container at /etc/blackbox/adilet_ca_bundle.pem
# (referenced by the http_2xx_adilet module's tls_config.ca_file in
# deploy/monitoring/blackbox/blackbox.yml, which IS committed).

The public certificate itself is already tracked in git at
`tools/legal_research/adilet_ca_bundle.pem` (added there for the lawyer
role's adilet.zan.kz TLS chain fix; `.pem` is gitignored in general but this
file was force-added — see CLAUDE.md). What was never recorded anywhere is
that the *same* file must be copied into the monitoring stack so blackbox_
exporter's http_2xx_adilet probe can validate adilet's certificate chain too
(same root cause: adilet's server sends an incomplete chain missing the
GoGetSSL intermediate).

Staging command run by hand on 2026-07-22 (idempotent, safe to re-run after
any rebuild of the monitoring host):

    sudo -u hermes cp \
      /home/hermes/.hermes/hermes-agent/tools/legal_research/adilet_ca_bundle.pem \
      /home/hermes/.hermes/monitoring/blackbox/adilet_ca_bundle.pem

If this file is ever rotated (e.g. GoGetSSL reissues), update the source
under tools/legal_research/ first, then re-run this copy — do not edit the
staged copy directly, it will drift silently.
